From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000026
Subject: [PATCH] vending, buyingstore: tell the dynamic market of trades with shells

The population engine's dynamic market moves an item's price index when a
player buys from a population shell's stall (up) or sells into a shell's
buying store (down). These are the two places that see those trades; each
hands the item, amount and price to population_engine_market_trade, which
does nothing while no mod has the market on. Trades between players, and
shells' own, are untouched.

--- a/src/map/vending.cpp
+++ b/src/map/vending.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "npc.hpp"
 #include "path.hpp"
 #include "pc.hpp"
+#include "population_engine.hpp"
 #include "pet.hpp"
 #include "pc_groups.hpp"
 
@@ -242,6 +243,9 @@
 			pc_additem(sd, &vsd->cart.u.items_cart[idx], amount, LOG_TYPE_VENDING);
 		vsd->vending[vend_list[i]].amount -= amount;
 		z += ((double)vsd->vending[vend_list[i]].value * (double)amount);
+		// RAGNAROKMAC: the dynamic market hears of a player buying from a shell.
+		if( IS_POPULATION_ENGINE_ACCOUNT_ID(vsd->status.account_id) && !IS_POPULATION_ENGINE_ACCOUNT_ID(sd->status.account_id) )
+			population_engine_market_trade( vsd->cart.u.items_cart[idx].nameid, amount, vsd->vending[vend_list[i]].value, 0 );
 
 			if( !IS_POPULATION_ENGINE_ACCOUNT_ID(vsd->status.account_id) ) {
 			if( vsd->vending[vend_list[i]].amount ) {
